      "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR addresses issue #63943 by fixing the Triton MoE naive block assignment to only be used for batch size 1.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe naive block assignment path in `_prepare_expert_assignment()` is taken when:\n```python\nnum_tokens * top_k_num * 4 <= global_num_experts\n```\n\nOn this path, every (token, expert) pair gets its own block, so an expert chosen by several tokens in the batch has its weights read once per pair. On bandwidth-limited GPUs (NVIDIA GB10 / DGX Spark with LPDDR5x), this causes 8% to 2x slower decode for device-resident weights.\n\n## Solution\n\nOnly use the naive block assignment when `num_tokens == 1`, where no two tokens can share an expert. This keeps the batch-1 optimization from #29354/#39016 while removing the repeated reads at 2-4 tokens.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Modified `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/fused_moe.py`: Changed the naive block assignment condition from `num_tokens * top_k_num * 4 <= global_num_experts` to `num_tokens == 1`\n\n## Testing\n\n- The fix is a minimal one-line condition change\n- Existing MoE tests should cover the functionality\n- The issue author has offered to test patches on GB10 hardware",
      "changedFiles": 1,
